{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>I will mention</b> — the poet's words. <b>Rahab</b> — it is Egypt, which is called Rahab, or Rahab of every nation, and it is in construct state, like ושכורת (and drunken) without ולא מיין, as if he said: I will mention Rahab of every nation that may be, and Babel with them; I will mention this to those who know like me, and also I will mention Philistia with Tyre." "And the meaning of <b>this one was born there</b> — that occasionally, few in many years, there is born among them a wise man known in his generation, who has a name."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 87, :notes {0 "The parsing of ושכורת ולא מיין references Isaiah 49:26, where the construct form lacks the expected intermediate word; Ibn Ezra draws the analogy to explain Rahab as construct rather than absolute."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:36:15.370479538Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}